{
  "wireMagic": "pb3",
  "pens": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wsWinStyles": [ {
  
  } ],
  "wpWinPositions": [ {
  
  } ],
  "events": [ {
    "tStartMs": 0,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey! This episode was sponsored by Head \u0026 Shoulders."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 5760,
    "dDurationMs": 7280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "A hundred and twenty-five million years ago in what is now China, dinosaurs walked the earth."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 14620,
    "dDurationMs": 3740,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and a few species of small feathered dinosaurs climbed trees"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 19120,
    "dDurationMs": 2180,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is Sinornithosaurus"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 21800,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Although they couldn't truly fly, they could glide, which helped them evade predators and catch prey"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 28820,
    "dDurationMs": 4760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What makes these dinosaurs unique is how well-preserved their fossils were."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 34600,
    "dDurationMs": 4140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Normally when you find a dinosaur it's just a pile of bones and that's all there is."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 38740,
    "dDurationMs": 4880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In between the feathers and the parts of the feather we saw little bits of skin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 43620,
    "dDurationMs": 5580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you can tell that they are skin - they're not just random bits of rock or broken up bone or something"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 49200,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because they have a particular kind of cells within the structure"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 52620,
    "dDurationMs": 4260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "which are just like the skin cells that we find in humans today"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 57540,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, my first thought when I saw these was this is dinosaur dandruff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 60860,
    "dDurationMs": 6540,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I was already planning to write the paper with the headline of we have discovered dinosaur dandruff,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 67400,
    "dDurationMs": 1400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I thought great."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 68800,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So these dinosaurs may have had the first known case of dandruff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 73920,
    "dDurationMs": 1780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it certainly wasn't the last"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 75700,
    "dDurationMs": 3660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Our skin cells are constantly replenishing themselves"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 79360,
    "dDurationMs": 4520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "in fact every second 500 new skin cells are created"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 83880,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and as they move up through the outer layer of your skin, the epidermis"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 87700,
    "dDurationMs": 5100,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They flatten out and harden until they fall off one by one"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 92800,
    "dDurationMs": 5640,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "In fact over your lifetime you will shed about a hundred pounds of dead skin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 98440,
    "dDurationMs": 5300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But we don't really notice this because skin falls off in such tiny microscopic pieces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 103740,
    "dDurationMs": 6440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "except for some people from some parts of the body skin comes off in larger flakes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 110180,
    "dDurationMs": 5120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "typically from the skin under the hair the scalp and this is what's known as dandruff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 115300,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now around half of everyone on earth suffers from it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 119540,
    "dDurationMs": 3500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So there are actually a lot of scientists who study this condition."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 123040,
    "dDurationMs": 4020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and I'm flying to Cincinnati to Head \u0026 Shoulders headquarters to visit their lab"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 128960,
    "dDurationMs": 840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 130560,
    "dDurationMs": 1500,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Do you need a break or something?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 132060,
    "dDurationMs": 3140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No, it's funny like 'cause I'm not really sure what I'm getting myself into right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 135200,
    "dDurationMs": 1120,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "No. No."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 136320,
    "dDurationMs": 3080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I am going to have my head swabbed"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 139400,
    "dDurationMs": 1480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Mm-hmm. You are"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 140880,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "What what is that all about? I mean, this is something you do to people all the time?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 144160,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, yeah. Every day."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 145540,
    "dDurationMs": 3580,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "--You're gonna cotton swab my scalp. --Yes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 149120,
    "dDurationMs": 3020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And we're looking for what？"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 152140,
    "dDurationMs": 6860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So we are gonna be looking for the malassezia that is on your scalp."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 159000,
    "dDurationMs": 2220,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Okay, so what do I need to do?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 161220,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So I need you to have a seat here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 164420,
    "dDurationMs": 2960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Let's see and I just put my head in here?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 167380,
    "dDurationMs": 4940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, put your head face forward. Okay. What I'm gonna do is I'm gonna part your hair."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 172320,
    "dDurationMs": 6020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So now I'm gonna take my swab I'm basically gonna grab off your scalp. Mm-hmm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 178340,
    "dDurationMs": 2300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So then what I do is I take this"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 180640,
    "dDurationMs": 4720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These are sticky plates here that I can plate the malassezia on"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 185360,
    "dDurationMs": 2040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and what I can do is I can add a stain"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 187400,
    "dDurationMs": 6900,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "throw this under the microscope and this is the individual cells of malassezia here."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 194300,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Malassezia globosa is a fungus that lives on your scalp"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 198380,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "it thrives in the warm moist environment under your hair"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 202840,
    "dDurationMs": 5800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and it is thought to be one of the causes of dandruff. So, how did my swab come back?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 208640,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well, I have malassezia living on my head."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 212120,
    "dDurationMs": 4300,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is actually what the fungus looks like. This is a lawn of the Malassezia globosa fungi."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 216420,
    "dDurationMs": 1680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You say a lawn. It's a lawn."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 218100,
    "dDurationMs": 3680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So basically you can see those little dots they're all individual colonies"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 221780,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and when they grow really close together like that, that's a lawn, Kind of like a bunch of grass"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 229180,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Now that I'm close to and actually smell it it smells like bread"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 232900,
    "dDurationMs": 1880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Yeah, well, you know, it's a yeast"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 234780,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": " You know it's a free, living fungus just like the Saccharomyces that are used to make bread and make beer with"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 240400,
    "dDurationMs": 1380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So, could you make bread with this?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 241780,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Uh.. No. I wouldn't want to make bread with the yeast off of your scalp. Not right now."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 247940,
    "dDurationMs": 3480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "-- Have you been tested? -- I've been tested. Yes. -- And what did it come out to?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 251420,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I have a decent amount. So... But we all do. So..."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 255420,
    "dDurationMs": 940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's on everyone's head."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 256360,
    "dDurationMs": 3040,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "It's on everyone's head as long as you have hair. --Right"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 259900,
    "dDurationMs": 4660,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if everyone has Malassezia, why do only half of us get dandruff?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 264560,
    "dDurationMs": 4960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Well Malassezia lives on the oils called sebum secreted by your skin"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 269520,
    "dDurationMs": 5020,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The fungi release enzymes called lipases that break down fat molecules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 274540,
    "dDurationMs": 3780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Oh, so this is one of the lipases that Malassezia produces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 278320,
    "dDurationMs": 3800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is something that Malassezia uses to get food"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 282120,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But unfortunately as a byproduct of that it also attacks your scalp"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 285840,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it produces free fatty acids that irritate the scalp"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 289840,
    "dDurationMs": 4560,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for some of us those molecules are perceived as invaders if you will"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 294400,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and all the defensive forces that we have will get turned on to repel essentially these invading molecules"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 301360,
    "dDurationMs": 4380,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and those defensive forces end up causing this collateral damage"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 305740,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that we interpret as an unhealthy scalp and dandruff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 309020,
    "dDurationMs": 4000,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "One of the scalps defenses is to speed up the turnover of skin cells"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 313020,
    "dDurationMs": 6160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So instead of taking a month for skin cells to mature and reach the surface they take as little as seven days"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 319180,
    "dDurationMs": 4620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "When you know they get to the surface the adhesive function from one cell to the other hasn't been lost"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 323800,
    "dDurationMs": 5780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so they shed as these clumps of skin cells three or four hundred together, which we see as a dandruff flake"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 330960,
    "dDurationMs": 5860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "the dandruff flakes are just an indicator of a fundamentally unhealthy scalp underlying it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 336820,
    "dDurationMs": 3160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "by any measure you can dream of making"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 339980,
    "dDurationMs": 4780,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Dandruff skin samples show elevated levels of inflammatory cytokines"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 344760,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Histamines which cause itching, and blood proteins on the surface of the scalp"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 349840,
    "dDurationMs": 6140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Indicating that the skin is not acting as a good barrier between your insides and the outside world"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 355980,
    "dDurationMs": 4400,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But it goes even further than that down to the level of gene expression"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 360380,
    "dDurationMs": 6140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Scientists took swabs from healthy scalps and dandruff scalps and then they extracted the RNA"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 366520,
    "dDurationMs": 4840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Effectively markers of which genes are being expressed and how strongly"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 371360,
    "dDurationMs": 1920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then they compared the two groups"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 373280,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and they found that there were nearly 4000 genes which were systematically"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 378140,
    "dDurationMs": 5360,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "either up-regulated or down-regulated in the dandruff scalps  compared to the healthy scalps"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 383500,
    "dDurationMs": 3840,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "for example immune and inflammatory response genes were up-regulated,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 387340,
    "dDurationMs": 4080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "things like lipid metabolism were down regulated and it all kind of makes sense"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 391420,
    "dDurationMs": 3860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But now that you know that there's a difference at the level of gene expression,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 395280,
    "dDurationMs": 2680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "How do you actually treat dandruff?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 397960,
    "dDurationMs": 3260,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is the the lawn of Malassezia."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 401220,
    "dDurationMs": 5140,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This is the Malassezia with a spot of the Head \u0026 Shoulders active put on it"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 406360,
    "dDurationMs": 4920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "The Malassezia just doesn't grow where that Head \u0026 Shoulders active actually is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 411280,
    "dDurationMs": 5620,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "These active ingredients can be zinc pyrithione, selenium sulfide, or piroctone olamine."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 416900,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They are controlling the metabolism of those Malassezia cells that are leading to irritating substances"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 423780,
    "dDurationMs": 3420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so the idea is to suppress their bio activity to some extent"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 427200,
    "dDurationMs": 3720,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so that we're reducing the level of irritating substances on our scalp"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 430920,
    "dDurationMs": 5060,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "that trigger the irritation and hyperproliferation and buried destruction that we talked about"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 435980,
    "dDurationMs": 4860,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "now that we understand like these clusters in these genes signatures of dandruff is"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 440840,
    "dDurationMs": 3200,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Can we reverse these gene signatures if we treat with Head \u0026 Shoulders?"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 444040,
    "dDurationMs": 4440,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So this is the group of dandruff at baseline and these genes are all down-regulated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 448480,
    "dDurationMs": 1800,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and then these genes are up-regulated"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 450280,
    "dDurationMs": 5700,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "You can see if you treat with just a cosmetic shampoo that you really don't make a difference in those genes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 455980,
    "dDurationMs": 2920,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But if you treat with Head \u0026 Shoulders after three weeks"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 458900,
    "dDurationMs": 4160,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "This signature looks just like somebody who doesn't have dandruff."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 463060,
    "dDurationMs": 4680,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And so you're looking at 3,700 genes have all clustered all on here,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 467740,
    "dDurationMs": 5080,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "And you're seeing them flip around. They're going from an unhealthy signature to a healthy signature"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 472820,
    "dDurationMs": 3820,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So Head \u0026 Shoulders reduces the Malassezia irritants on the scalp,"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 476640,
    "dDurationMs": 4240,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "changing your scalp‘s response, and ultimately reducing skin flakes"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 480880,
    "dDurationMs": 3320,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So unlike dinosaurs, we don't have to live with dandruff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 484980,
    "dDurationMs": 5760,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But in their case the presence of skin flakes reveals something important about their biology"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 490740,
    "dDurationMs": 5520,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "They had evolved warm-bloodedness and hence feathers as a way to keep warm"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 496260,
    "dDurationMs": 6880,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "But once they had feathers skin could no longer be shed in one piece like a snake but instead in tiny pieces"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 503140,
    "dDurationMs": 6960,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "So in fact, although it's an amusing discovery it actually had quite an important or profound point"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 510100,
    "dDurationMs": 4480,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "because it tells us that dinosaurs while commonly called reptiles"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 514580,
    "dDurationMs": 5420,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "are on the side of the birds and the mammals in terms of physiology. They were definitely warm-blooded"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 522700,
    "dDurationMs": 4460,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "Hey, I hope you learned something from watching this video I certainly learned a lot making it."
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 527160,
    "dDurationMs": 3940,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "and if you want to find out more about Head \u0026 Shoulders research or about how to get rid of dandruff"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 531100,
    "dDurationMs": 2690,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "I will put a link to their website down in the description"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 533790,
    "dDurationMs": 4150,
    "segs": [ {
      "utf8": "so I want to say a big thanks to Head \u0026 Shoulders for supporting this episode of Veritasium"
    } ]
  }, {
    "tStartMs": 537940,
    "dDurationMs": 3280,
